  "id": "DrugBank_DB00736 - MONDO_2177",
  "verbalization": "Esomeprazole, a proton pump inhibitor, is implicated in the pathogenesis of Hyperinsulinism (disease) through a chain of indications involving Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome and other drugs. The evidence suggests that Esomeprazole is linked to Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome, which in turn is associated with the use of Cimetidine and Dexrabeprazole, both of which are indicated for Hyperinsulinism. This suggests a potential mechanism where the gastrointestinal disturbances caused by Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome may influence insulin secretion or metabolism, leading to hyperinsulinism. The recurring link between these entities implies a possible role of proton pump inhibitors in modulating gastrointestinal function, which could indirectly affect insulin regulation. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, highlighting a possible pathway involving gastrointestinal dysfunction and insulin dysregulation.",
